838 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 750 0 R
/T (Current digital tools for dyslexia are mostly single-player, focusing only on decoding accuracy while ignoring social and emotional needs. They rely on post-error feedback that reinforces failure. No existing system combines multiplayer collaboration, cross-device interaction \(mobile + PC\), and voice-enabled peer communication in a literacy game designed specifically for dyslexic children.)
/E (Current digital tools for dyslexia are mostly single-player, focusing only on decoding accuracy while ignoring social and emotional needs. They rely on post-error feedback that reinforces failure. No existing system combines multiplayer collaboration, cross-device interaction \(mobile + PC\), and voice-enabled peer communication in a literacy game designed specifically for dyslexic children.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
839 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 750 0 R
/T (No game-based solution exists that targets these social dimensions. On the technology side, no system combines multiplayer + multimodal + dual-device \(mobile + PC\) interaction for dyslexic children. Tools rely heavily on post-error feedback, lack voice-enabled peer interaction, and ignore social confidence entirely.)
/E (No game-based solution exists that targets these social dimensions. On the technology side, no system combines multiplayer + multimodal + dual-device \(mobile + PC\) interaction for dyslexic children. Tools rely heavily on post-error feedback, lack voice-enabled peer interaction, and ignore social confidence entirely.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
